# Applied by Cloudflare to the static pages and files. (Worker responses, such as /admin and /api, set their own.)
# The Content-Security-Policy is not here: Astro writes it into each page as a <meta> tag, with the hashes of the
# page's inline scripts (`security.csp` in astro.config.mjs). A <meta> policy cannot set frame-ancestors, so
# X-Frame-Options below is what stops other sites from framing the pages.
# No Strict-Transport-Security yet: add it once the production domain is on HTTPS for good (it is hard to undo).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
